    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-xs text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Card 1: Capacitive DBD Physics -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">1</span>
          Capacitive Dielectric Barrier Physics
        </h3>
        <p>
          Dielectric barrier discharge (DBD) inserts high-permittivity insulating layers (quartz or alumina, &epsilon;_r &approx; 4.5&ndash;9.8) between metal electrodes to prevent thermal arc transition. Under sinusoidal or pulsed excitation (V = 10&ndash;30 kV, f = 15&ndash;45 kHz), charge accumulates on the dielectric surface, generating self-terminating nanosecond micro-discharges across the gas gap.
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          E_gap = (V_applied / d_gap) &times; [&epsilon;_diel / (&epsilon;_diel + 2d_diel/d_gap)]
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          Electric field strength (E &gt; 25 kV/cm) accelerates electrons to mean energies of 1.5&ndash;4.8 eV while bulk gas temperature remains near ambient (T_gas &lt; 28&deg;C).
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 2: Aerosol Micro-Mist Radical Synthesis -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">2</span>
          Electron Impact &amp; Aerosol RONS Kinetics
        </h3>
        <p>
          High-energy plasma electrons collide with water aerosol micro-droplets (D32 &approx; 5&ndash;25 &mu;m) and ambient carrier molecules (N2, O2), triggering instant electron impact dissociation and charge transfer:
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          e⁻ + H₂O &rarr; &bull;OH + H&bull; + e⁻ (k &approx; 1.2 &times; 10⁻¹⁰ cm³/s)<br/>
          &bull;NO + O₂&bull;⁻ &rarr; ONOO⁻ (peroxynitrite synthesis)<br/>
          &bull;OH + &bull;OH &rarr; H₂O₂ (dissolved persistent oxidant)
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          Hydroxyl radicals (&bull;OH, oxidation potential E&deg; = 2.80 V) and peroxynitrite (ONOO⁻, E&deg; = 2.05 V) dissolve instantaneously into micro-droplets following Henry's law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 3: Interfacial Droplet Mass Transfer -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">3</span>
          Sub-15 µm Micro-Droplet Penetration
        </h3>
        <p>
          Conventional water washing fails because surface tension (&gamma; &approx; 72.8 mN/m) and hydrophobic cuticular waxes prevent immersion liquid from entering produce stomata (5&ndash;15 &mu;m) and netting crevasses.
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          a_specific = 6 / D32 (m&sup2;/m&sup3;)<br/>
          Sh = 2.0 + 0.6 &times; Re^(1/2) &times; Sc^(1/3)
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          Sub-15 &mu;m aerosol droplets exhibit ultra-high specific surface area (a &gt; 400,000 m&sup2;/m&sup3;) and enter stomatal openings without hydraulic wetting or capillary waterlogging.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 4: Multi-Pathogen Cell Lysis -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">4</span>
          Cellular Lysis &amp; Viral Capsid Oxidation
        </h3>
        <p>
          RONS attack outer cell envelopes via lipid peroxidation: hydroxyl radicals abstract hydrogen atoms from polyunsaturated acyl chains of phospholipid bilayers, forming hydroperoxides (LOOH) that destabilize membrane permeability.
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          Log(N/N₀) = - (t / &delta;)^p (Weibull Inactivation)
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          For non-enveloped viral surrogates (Murine Norovirus MNV-1), singlet oxygen (&sup1;O₂) and peroxynitrite degrade VP1 protein coat capsids, destroying host-cell binding ligands.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 5: Produce Quality Preservation -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">5</span>
          PPO Inhibition &amp; Turgor Retention
        </h3>
        <p>
          Enzymatic browning on cut produce is driven by polyphenol oxidase (PPO). Plasma-generated nitric oxide (&bull;NO) and nitrite ions competitively coordinate with binuclear copper active sites (CuA, CuB), suppressing melanosis by &gt;90%.
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          Firmness_Retention = 100 - [k_wilt &times; (T - 25&deg;C) + k_arc &times; E]
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          Because total water deposition is less than 0.003 L/kg, cellular pectin middle lamella remains intact, preserving natural crispness without chemical calcium dips.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Card 6: Regulatory Compliance -->
      <article class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-hairline space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-5 h-5 rounded-md bg-cyan-950 text-cyan-300 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-[10px] border border-cyan-800">6</span>
          FSMA, USDA GAP &amp; 3-A Standards
        </h3>
        <p>
          Complies with FDA Food Safety Modernization Act (FSMA 21 CFR § 112) for post-harvest agricultural water contact and sanitation, USDA-AMS Harmonized GAP Plus+, and 3-A Sanitary Standards 42-02 &amp; 74-07.
        </p>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-lg bg-surface-soft font-mono text-[11px] border border-hairline/60 text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">
          OSHA PEL: [O₃]_ambient &lt; 0.10 ppm (8h TWA)<br/>
          Skid Effluent: [O₃] &lt; 0.02 ppm (MnO₂ Scrubber)
        </div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">
          The catalytic manganese dioxide destruct unit prevents ozone off-gas venting, satisfying OSHA 29 CFR 1910.1000 workplace indoor air criteria.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

